<Base title="Photo & artwork credits — Kartik Tagore" description="Credits and licenses for photographs used in Kartik Tagore's personal website.">
  <article class="paper-document">
    <a class="breadcrumb" href="/">← Back to the workbench</a>
    <header class="article-head"><p class="eyebrow">Sources & thanks</p><h1>Photo & artwork credits</h1><p class="lede">Original sources behind the photographs and published illustrations.</p></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>McQueen photography is from <a href="https://blog.sravjti.in/2026/10/20/mcqueen.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SRA VJTI's build article</a>, credited to the project team. The original SVGs are artwork created for this site.</p>
      <p>Curated public-domain and CC0 illustrations, when downloaded: <a href="https://freesvg.org/dumbbell-drawing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenClipart dumbbell drawing</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soccerball.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenClipart soccer ball</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volleyball_(transparent).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Angelo Gelmi / Svgalbertian / Luan volleyball</a>; <a href="https://freesvg.org/shuttlecock" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">gnokii-based shuttlecock</a>; <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chess_white_knight.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CyrilKato / Sashité chess knight</a>; and <a href="https://freesvg.org/paddle" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenClipart table-tennis paddles</a>. The vector originals are publicly available artworks, not AI-rendered substitutes.</p>
      <p>The helmet, Arduino UNO and Jetson images were supplied for the site. The site owner confirms permission to publish them.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
